1
00:00:00,019 --> 00:00:03,596
Today's Mars maps are global. Astronauts will walk a few kilometres.

2
00:00:03,646 --> 00:00:07,205
MarsWalk zooms to walking scale: Curiosity's real 2025 boxwork route on Mount Sharp.

3
00:00:07,255 --> 00:00:10,937
Pick a science target: Monte Grande Hollow & Nevado Sajama Ridge, where Curiosity drilled a ridge and a hollow.

4
00:00:10,987 --> 00:00:14,557
It checks the crew: 655 kcal, 0.20 kg of oxygen, cooling water, radiation, daylight and the turn-back point.

5
00:00:14,607 --> 00:00:18,506
One click prints the EVA cue card: timeline, stations, oxygen left, GO / NO-GO.

6
00:00:18,556 --> 00:00:23,037
Then the crew walks it, with a visor HUD that counts down time, oxygen and the way home.

7
00:00:23,087 --> 00:00:28,260
…and rehearses it on the real terrain in 3D before ever leaving the habitat.

8
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,950
MarsWalk: plan it, brief it, walk it. Works offline, because Mars has no internet.
